  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Grounding by construction",
      "items": [
        "The composer names evidence refs; code copies name, address, price, hours and sources.",
        "A named place outside the atlas is looked up (Google Places live, Wikipedia offline) before it is added.",
        "If no source exists and the traveller insists, the stop is added marked unconfirmed, with a visible gap.",
        "A deterministic budget guard trims paid stops rather than letting the total overrun."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "State and edits",
      "items": [
        "Plans are append-only versions; restore copies an old version forward.",
        "An edit returns typed ops and a proposal; the plan changes only when a tick is accepted.",
        "Locked and confirmed stops are never moved or removed by an edit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Security and trust",
      "items": [
        "The traveller message is untrusted data in every prompt; injection is recorded as a threat.",
        "A canary is checked on every model output; a leak becomes a refusal.",
        "Code chooses which provider runs: no booking or payment tool exists.",
        "Session access: owner token, signed-in user, or local admin."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Evaluation",
      "items": [
        "The 7 frozen v4 suites run through the same orchestrator with sandbox evidence.",
        "Scoring is deterministic: intent match, constraint audit, source coverage, disruption outcome.",
        "Runs and scores persist to SQLite and export from the Evaluation tab."
      ]
    }
  ]
